This script adds custom buttons to the Sales Invoice form that allow users to get items from Healthcare Services, Prescriptions, and Vaccinations. When the buttons are clicked, a dialog is presented to the user to select the relevant items, which are then added to the Sales Invoice.

i need code in termain to replace in all files  "erpnext.healthcare." with "pets_healthcare."
ChatGPT
To replace all instances of "erpnext.healthcare." with "pets_healthcare." in all files within a directory and its subdirectories, you can use the find command along with sed. Here is the command you can use in your terminal:

bash
Copy code
find /path/to/your/directory -type f -exec sed -i 's/erpnext\.healthcare\./pets_healthcare\./g' {} +
Explanation:
find /path/to/your/directory: This command starts a search from the specified directory (/path/to/your/directory). Replace this with the actual path to your directory.
-type f: This option ensures that the search is only for files.
-exec sed -i 's/erpnext\.healthcare\./pets_healthcare\./g' {} +: This part executes the sed command to perform the search and replace within each file found.
sed -i: This option edits the files in place.
's/erpnext\.healthcare\./pets_healthcare\./g': This is the substitution command in sed. It replaces all instances (g flag) of erpnext.healthcare. with pets_healthcare.. The backslashes (\) are used to escape the dots (.), which are special characters in regular expressions.
{} is a placeholder for the current file name.
+ ensures that sed is called with multiple files at once for efficiency.
Note:
Ensure you have a backup of your files before running this command, as it will make changes directly to the files.
Replace /path/to/your/directory with the actual path to the directory where you want to perform the replacement.
